SEC. 60001: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available for the Clean Heavy-Duty Vehicle program under Section 132 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7432), eliminating the remaining funding for that initiative.

SEC. 60002: Repeals Section 134 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7434), which established the Greenhouse Gas Reduction Fund, and rescinds all unobligated balances of amounts made available for that section as in effect before enactment.

SEC. 60003: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60104 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2067), which provided funding for diesel emissions reductions.

SEC. 60004: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60105 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2067), which provided funding to address air pollution.

SEC. 60005: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60106 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2069), which provided funding to address air pollution at schools.

SEC. 60006: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 135 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7435), which established the Low Emissions Electricity Program.

SEC. 60007: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60108 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2070), which funded implementation of Section 211(o) of the Clean Air Act (renewable fuel standards).

SEC. 60008: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60109 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2071), which funded implementation of the American Innovation and Manufacturing Act.

SEC. 60009: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60110 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2071), which funded enforcement technology and public information activities.

SEC. 60010: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60111 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2072), which funded greenhouse gas corporate reporting requirements.

SEC. 60011: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60112 of Public Law 117-169 (42 U.S.C. 4321 note; 136 Stat. 2072), which funded environmental product declaration assistance.

SEC. 60012: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available for the methane emissions and waste reduction incentive program for petroleum and natural gas systems under subsections (a) and (b) of Section 136 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7436). Additionally, amends Section 136(g) of the Clean Air Act to extend the program's authorization period from "calendar year 2024" to "calendar year 2034."

SEC. 60013: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 137 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7437), which funded greenhouse gas air pollution plans and implementation grants.

SEC. 60014: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60115 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2077), which funded Environmental Protection Agency efficient, accurate, and timely reviews.

SEC. 60015: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60116 of Public Law 117-169 (42 U.S.C. 4321 note; 136 Stat. 2077), which funded low-embodied carbon labeling for construction materials.

SEC. 60016: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 138 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7438), which established the Environmental and Climate Justice Block Grants program.

SEC. 60017: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60301 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2079), which funded ESA (Endangered Species Act) recovery plans.

SEC. 60018: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60401 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2079), which funded environmental and climate data collection.

SEC. 60019: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 177 of title 23, United States Code, which established the Neighborhood Access and Equity Grant Program.

SEC. 60020: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60502 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083), which funded Federal building assistance.

SEC. 60021: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60503 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083), which funded low-carbon materials for Federal buildings.

SEC. 60022: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60504 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083), which funded GSA emerging and sustainable technologies.

SEC. 60023: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 178 of title 23, United States Code, which funded environmental review implementation.

SEC. 60024: Rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 179 of title 23, United States Code, which funded low-carbon transportation materials grants.

SEC. 60025: Appropriates $256,657,000 for fiscal year 2025, out of any money in the Treasury not otherwise appropriated, to remain available until September 30, 2029, for necessary expenses for capital repair, restoration, maintenance backlog, and security structures of the building and site of the John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts. Not more than 3 percent of these funds may be used for administrative costs.

SEC. 60026: Amends Title I of the National Environmental Policy Act of 1969 (42 U.S.C. 4331 et seq.) by adding a new Section 112, which establishes a process for project sponsors to opt into paying fees for environmental reviews. Under this process, a project sponsor submits a project description and declaration of intent to prepare the environmental assessment or environmental impact statement under Section 107(f); the Council on Environmental Quality must provide notice of the fee amount within 15 days; and the fee is set at 125 percent of the anticipated costs to prepare or supervise preparation of the review. For projects with paid fees, an environmental assessment must be completed within 180 days of fee payment, and an environmental impact statement must be completed within 1 year of the notice of intent publication. [end of text]


